{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L1.001","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write exactly one coherent English paragraph of 60-100 words explaining why bees are important to ecosystems. Use complete sentences and include at least one specific ecological role of bees, such as pollination, supporting plant reproduction, biodiversity, or food webs. Do not use bullet points, headings, markdown, or blank lines. Count words by spaces. Output only the paragraph.","ground_truth":"<Exactly one coherent English paragraph of 60-100 space-delimited words. It uses complete sentences and explains at least one specific ecological role of bees, such as pollination, plant reproduction, biodiversity, or food-web support.>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 only if all conditions hold; otherwise score 0. (a) The output contains exactly one nonempty paragraph, with no blank lines, bullets, heading, or markdown formatting. (b) It contains 60-100 words under whitespace-delimited word counting. (c) It consists of complete English sentences and has no obvious grammar, spelling, or punctuation errors that materially impair readability. (d) It is coherent and does not mechanically repeat a sentence or the same claim. (e) It explains at least one specific ecological contribution of bees, such as pollination, plant reproduction, biodiversity, or support for food webs. Do not require every example listed, a particular wording, or a particular number of sentences."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L1.002","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a single paragraph of 60-100 words describing the experience of watching a sunrise from a quiet beach. Use complete sentences and varied sentence structures. Do not use lists, headings, or markdown. Output only the paragraph.","ground_truth":"A coherent, fluent English description of watching a sunrise from a quiet beach, using complete sentences and more than one sentence pattern. The requested single paragraph, 60–100-word range, and plain-prose presentation are target presentation guidance rather than sole capability-failure conditions.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_prose_rubric","core_requirements":["Substantially describes the experience of watching a sunrise from a quiet beach.","Uses complete, generally grammatical English that is fluent and readily comprehensible.","Shows meaningful sentence-pattern or sentence-length variation."],"presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: one plain-prose paragraph of 60–100 words with no surrounding labels or Markdown."],"category_policy":"This is an output capability probe, not instr. Do not fail solely for ordinary word-count, paragraph-count, plain-text, or output-only deviation when the core prose capability is clearly demonstrated."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a material topic, voice, fluency, coherence, or requested-genre failure. Do not fail solely for ordinary presentation or length deviation outside category instr."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":"Scoring note: separates core prose capability from non-instr presentation diagnostics."}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L1.003","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a single paragraph (60-100 words) explaining the basic concept of supply and demand for a non-economist reader. Define both terms and briefly explain how their interaction affects market prices or quantities. Use complete sentences. No bullets, headings, or markdown. Output only the paragraph.","ground_truth":"<One coherent English paragraph of 60-100 words. It should explain supply as the amount sellers/producers are willing or able to offer and demand as the amount buyers/consumers are willing or able to buy, and state that their interaction generally influences price and/or quantity. Equivalent plain-language wording is acceptable.>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) exactly one paragraph, with no blank lines, bullets, headings, or markdown; (b) 60-100 English words inclusive; (c) complete, readable sentences with no serious or repeated grammar/spelling errors; (d) coherent prose without obvious repetition; (e) uses jargon-free language suitable for a non-economist; (f) correctly identifies supply as what sellers/producers offer and demand as what buyers/consumers seek to buy, and explains that their interaction generally affects market price and/or quantity. Accept minor simplifications that do not reverse or materially distort these concepts. Do not require a specific example, equilibrium terminology, or a fixed causal formulation."],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L1.004","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a single paragraph (60-100 words) reflecting on what makes a good neighbor. Use complete sentences. No lists, headings, or markdown. Output only the paragraph.","ground_truth":"开放式答案：接受任何仅包含一个连贯英文段落、按空白分隔计为 60-100 个英文词、使用完整且可理解的句子、内容反思好邻居应具备的品质，并且不含列表、标题、Markdown、空行或其他额外文本的回答。","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output contains exactly one non-empty paragraph, with no blank lines, bullets, headings, markdown, or extra commentary; (b) the paragraph contains 60-100 English words inclusive, counted by whitespace-separated tokens; (c) it is written in complete, understandable sentences with no obvious grammar or spelling problems that impair readability; (d) it reflects on qualities or behaviors that make someone a good neighbor. Do not require sentence-length or syntactic variation beyond the prompt."],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L1.005","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a single paragraph (60-100 words) for a museum placard about the invention of the printing press. Use complete sentences in a neutral, informative tone. No bullets or headings. Output only the paragraph.","ground_truth":"<A single coherent English paragraph of 60–100 words, using complete sentences and a neutral, informative museum-placard tone, that describes the invention or early development of the printing press. No bullets, heading, or extra text.>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output consists of exactly one paragraph, with no blank lines, bullets, headings, or extra text; (b) it contains 60–100 words inclusive; (c) it uses complete, clearly intelligible standard-English sentences, with no obvious grammar or spelling errors that impair readability or a professional placard tone; consistent British or American spelling is acceptable; (d) it has a neutral, informative museum-placard tone, not casual, promotional, or conversational; (e) it substantively describes the invention or early development of the printing press, optionally including its historical impact. Do not penalize minor historical inaccuracies; assess format, fluency, tone, and topical fulfillment rather than factual precision."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L2.001","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 3-paragraph essay (each paragraph 50-80 words) on the benefits of reading fiction. Use smooth transition phrases between paragraphs. Plain prose only — no headings, bullets, or markdown. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the essay; no preamble, intro line, or sign-off.","ground_truth":"<Exactly 3 English prose paragraphs; each contains 50–80 words inclusive; paragraphs are separated by exactly one empty line; paragraph 2 and paragraph 3 each contain a clear transition that semantically continues the preceding paragraph; discusses benefits of reading fiction; no title, heading, preamble, sign-off, bullets, Markdown, or non-essay text.>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output consists of exactly 3 prose paragraphs, separated by exactly one empty line (two newline characters) and contains no other text before or after them; (b) each paragraph contains 50–80 words inclusive; (c) there are no headings, bullets, numbering, code fences, block quotes, links, emphasis markers, or other Markdown/structured formatting; (d) paragraph 2 and paragraph 3 each include a clear transition phrase, preferably in the opening sentence, that semantically connects to the preceding paragraph; (e) all paragraphs remain focused on benefits of reading fiction; (f) prose has no material grammar or spelling errors that impair fluency or readability. Minor stylistic variation is acceptable."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L2.002","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 3-paragraph briefing (each paragraph 50-80 words) for a city council on the value of public libraries. Use smooth transitions between paragraphs. Plain prose only. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the briefing; no preamble or sign-off.","ground_truth":"必须仅输出一篇关于公共图书馆价值、面向市议会的正式简报正文：恰好3个段落，段落之间恰有一个空行；每段50–80个英文单词；不得有标题、项目符号、前言、元评论、签名或落款；使用纯散文；段落之间应有清晰的逻辑衔接；内容应具体说明公共图书馆的公共价值。","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output contains exactly 3 prose paragraphs separated by exactly one blank line, with no heading, bullet list, preamble, meta-commentary, sign-off, or other non-briefing text; (b) each paragraph contains 50–80 English words; (c) the text is a formal city-council briefing that substantively explains the value of public libraries; (d) adjacent paragraphs have clear logical continuity, through explicit transition language or natural semantic linkage; (e) language is professional and has no material grammar or spelling errors that impair readability. Otherwise score 0."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L2.003","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 3-paragraph review of a fictional restaurant called 'The Copper Pot'. Each paragraph must contain 50-80 words. Ensure the paragraphs flow naturally into one another. Use plain prose only: no title, headings, bullets, preamble, or sign-off. Separate paragraphs with exactly one blank line. Output only the review.","ground_truth":"<A valid response is an on-topic review of the fictional restaurant 'The Copper Pot' consisting of exactly 3 prose paragraphs. Each paragraph has 50-80 whitespace-delimited words. Paragraphs are separated by exactly one blank line and connect naturally through transition wording or clear semantic continuity. The response contains no title, headings, bullets, preamble, sign-off, or unrelated meta-text, and has no obvious errors that materially impair readability.>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) the response contains exactly 3 prose paragraphs separated by exactly one blank line; (b) each paragraph contains 50-80 whitespace-delimited words; (c) it is an on-topic review of the fictional restaurant 'The Copper Pot'; (d) the paragraphs have natural continuity, through transition language or clear semantic connection; (e) it contains no title, headings, bullets, preamble, sign-off, or unrelated meta-text; and (f) it has no obvious grammar or spelling errors that materially impair readability. Do not require specific transition phrases or wording."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L2.004","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 3-paragraph cover letter excerpt (each paragraph 50-80 words) for a graphic-design role at a fictional studio called 'Lumen Studio'. Use smooth transitions between paragraphs. Plain prose only — no headings, bullets, or salutations. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the excerpt; no preamble or sign-off.","ground_truth":"<恰好 3 段；段间仅一个空行；每段 50–80 个英文单词；纯正文，无标题、称呼、项目符号、前言或落款；专业求职语体；内容提及 graphic design 和 Lumen Studio；段落间有自然、连贯的过渡>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output contains exactly 3 prose paragraphs separated by exactly one blank line, with no headings, salutations, bullets, preamble, sign-off, or other extra text; (b) each paragraph contains 50-80 English words; (c) the paragraphs have clear, natural semantic transitions, whether through explicit connectives or coherent reference/continuation; (d) writing is professional cover-letter prose with no obvious grammar or spelling errors that materially reduce quality; (e) content is relevant to a graphic-design role and explicitly mentions Lumen Studio."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L2.005","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 3-paragraph informative piece (each paragraph 50–80 words, counted by whitespace-separated words) explaining how composting works at home for an interested beginner. Cover what materials to add, how to maintain the pile, and how to recognize or use finished compost. Use clear, natural transitions between paragraphs. Plain prose only. Separate adjacent paragraphs with exactly one blank line. Output only the piece, with no title, preamble, or sign-off.","ground_truth":"<Exactly 3 prose paragraphs, with exactly one blank line between adjacent paragraphs and no title/preamble/sign-off. Each paragraph contains 50–80 whitespace-separated words. The piece clearly explains home composting for a beginner, including suitable materials, basic maintenance (moisture and airflow/turning), and finished-compost use or recognition. Paragraphs have natural logical transitions.>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output contains exactly 3 prose paragraphs, with exactly one blank line between adjacent paragraphs, and contains no heading, bullet list, preamble, or sign-off; (b) each paragraph has 50–80 whitespace-separated words; (c) the paragraphs have clear natural logical continuity, whether achieved through explicit transition words, reference, sequencing, cause-and-effect, or other coherent discourse devices; (d) the explanation is understandable for an interested beginner and accurately describes home composting, including suitable inputs, moisture/airflow maintenance, and finished-compost use or recognition; (e) it contains no material factual errors and no grammar or spelling errors that substantially impair fluency or comprehension."],"fail_criteria":["Fail if any mandatory task or pass criterion is unsatisfied, or if any rejection, forbidden, or failure condition stated inside a criterion is triggered."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L3.001","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 5-paragraph travel article (250-400 words total) about visiting a small coastal town. Maintain a consistent first-person reflective voice throughout. Vary sentence length and structure across paragraphs. Plain prose only — no headings, bullets, or markdown. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the article; no preamble or sign-off.","ground_truth":"A coherent travel article about visiting a small coastal town in a consistent first-person reflective voice, with varied sentence structure and fluent prose. Five paragraphs, 250–400 words, single blank-line separators, and plain-prose-only output are target presentation guidance.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_prose_rubric","core_requirements":["Is substantially an on-topic travel article about visiting a small coastal town.","Maintains a coherent first-person reflective perspective; an occasional sentence without an explicit first-person pronoun is natural.","Shows noticeable sentence-length and syntactic variation across the article.","Is fluent and has no material grammar or spelling errors that impair comprehension."],"presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: five plain-prose paragraphs, 250–400 words, separated by single blank lines, with no preamble or sign-off."],"category_policy":"This is an output capability probe, not instr. Do not fail solely for ordinary word-count, paragraph-count, plain-text, or output-only deviation when the core prose capability is clearly demonstrated."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a material topic, voice, fluency, coherence, or requested-genre failure. Do not fail solely for ordinary presentation or length deviation outside category instr."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":"Scoring note: separates core prose capability from non-instr presentation diagnostics."}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L3.002","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 5-paragraph opinion column (250-400 words total) arguing that public parks improve civic life. Maintain a consistent persuasive third-person voice. Vary sentence length and structure. Plain prose only — no headings, bullets, or markdown. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the column; no preamble or sign-off.","ground_truth":"A coherent persuasive column arguing that public parks improve civic life, predominantly in third person, with varied sentence structure and fluent prose. Five paragraphs, 250–400 words, and plain-prose-only output are target presentation guidance; an isolated rhetorical imperative is not a sustained voice shift.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_prose_rubric","core_requirements":["Presents a coherent, persuasive argument that public parks improve civic life.","Uses a predominantly consistent third-person persuasive voice without a sustained first-person or second-person shift.","Shows clear sentence-length and syntactic variation.","Is grammatical, readable, and professionally comprehensible."],"presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: five plain-prose paragraphs and 250–400 words with no preamble or sign-off.","An isolated rhetorical imperative such as 'Consider' does not by itself constitute sustained direct address."],"category_policy":"This is an output capability probe, not instr. Do not fail solely for ordinary word-count, paragraph-count, plain-text, or output-only deviation when the core prose capability is clearly demonstrated."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a material topic, voice, fluency, coherence, or requested-genre failure. Do not fail solely for ordinary presentation or length deviation outside category instr."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":"Scoring note: separates core prose capability from non-instr presentation diagnostics."}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L3.003","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 5-paragraph profile (250-400 words total) of a fictional luthier named Mara Devlin who builds violins in a small mountain workshop. Maintain a consistent observational third-person voice. Vary sentence length and structure. Plain prose only — no headings, bullets, or markdown. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the profile; no preamble or sign-off.","ground_truth":"An on-topic, fluent profile of fictional luthier Mara Devlin building violins in a small mountain workshop, in a consistent observational third-person voice with varied sentences. Five paragraphs, 250–400 words, and plain-prose-only output are target presentation guidance.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_prose_rubric","core_requirements":["Profiles the fictional luthier Mara Devlin and explicitly portrays her building violins in a small mountain workshop.","Maintains a coherent observational third-person narration without a sustained perspective shift.","Shows noticeable sentence-length and syntactic variation.","Is fluent and has no material grammar or spelling errors that impair professionalism."],"presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: five plain-prose paragraphs and 250–400 words with no title, preamble, or sign-off."],"category_policy":"This is an output capability probe, not instr. Do not fail solely for ordinary word-count, paragraph-count, plain-text, or output-only deviation when the core prose capability is clearly demonstrated."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a material topic, voice, fluency, coherence, or requested-genre failure. Do not fail solely for ordinary presentation or length deviation outside category instr."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":"Scoring note: separates core prose capability from non-instr presentation diagnostics."}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L3.004","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 5-paragraph short essay (250-400 words total) on the experience of learning a second language as an adult. Maintain a consistent first-person reflective voice. Vary sentence length and structure. Plain prose only — no headings, bullets, or markdown. Separate paragraphs with a single blank line. Output only the essay; no preamble or sign-off.","ground_truth":"<仅包含一篇关于成年人学习第二语言体验的英文短文；恰好 5 个段落，段落间恰有一个空白行；总计 250–400 词；全程采用一致的第一人称反思性叙述；句长和句法结构有可见变化；纯散文，不含标题、项目符号、Markdown、前言或署名。>","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":["Score 1 iff ALL hold: (a) output contains only an essay, with exactly 5 nonempty prose paragraphs separated by exactly one blank line; it contains no title, preamble, sign-off, bullets, headings, Markdown, or code formatting; (b) total word count is 250-400 under ordinary whitespace-delimited counting; (c) the essay is substantively about the writer's experience of learning a second language as an adult; (d) it consistently uses a first-person reflective perspective; (e) sentence length and syntax show clear variation rather than repeated use of one simple sentence pattern; (f) language is generally grammatical and fluent, with no errors that materially impair readability or meaning."],"fail_criteria":["Any required format, length, content, tone, perspective, or fluency condition is not met."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.fluent_prose.L3.005","canonical_id":"output.fluent_prose","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"discourse_length":"multi_paragraph"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a 5-paragraph piece of historically plausible fictional prose (250-400 words total) about daily life in a small medieval European village. Use a consistent third-person, past-tense narrative voice. Include a noticeable mix of short and longer sentences and more than one sentence structure. Use plain prose only: no title, headings, bullets, markdown, preamble, or sign-off. Separate each paragraph with exactly one blank line. Output only the piece.","ground_truth":"Fluent, historically plausible fictional prose about daily life in a small medieval European village, predominantly in third-person past tense, with varied sentence length and structure. Five paragraphs, 250–400 words, and plain-prose-only output are target presentation guidance.","scorer":{"type":"judge_rubric","rubric":{"version":"1","pass_criteria":[{"type":"capability_prose_rubric","core_requirements":["Substantially depicts daily life in a small medieval European village without material anachronism or factual implausibility.","Uses a predominantly consistent third-person, past-tense narrative voice; brief natural dialogue is allowed.","Shows a noticeable mix of sentence lengths and at least two sentence structures.","Is fluent and has no material grammar or spelling errors that impair readability."],"presentation_preferences_nonbinding_in_capability_mode":["Target: five plain-prose paragraphs and 250–400 words with no title, preamble, or sign-off."],"category_policy":"This is an output capability probe, not instr. Do not fail solely for ordinary word-count, paragraph-count, plain-text, or output-only deviation when the core prose capability is clearly demonstrated."}],"fail_criteria":["Fail for a material topic, voice, fluency, coherence, or requested-genre failure. Do not fail solely for ordinary presentation or length deviation outside category instr."],"pass_rule":"all pass criteria and no fail criteria"}},"tags":["judge_required"],"notes":"Scoring note: separates core prose capability from non-instr presentation diagnostics."}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L1.001","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"plain_text_only"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that creates an xlsx file at the given `path` using `openpyxl`. The workbook has exactly one sheet named 'Data' with these cell values: A1='Name', B1='Score', A2='Alice', B2=42 (integer). Output ONLY the function definition inside a single fenced code block tagged `python`. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    from openpyxl import Workbook\n\n    wb = Workbook()\n    ws = wb.active\n    ws.title = \"Data\"\n    ws[\"A1\"] = \"Name\"\n    ws[\"B1\"] = \"Score\"\n    ws[\"A2\"] = \"Alice\"\n    ws[\"B2\"] = 42\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","sheet_names":["Data"],"cells":{"Data":{"A1":"Name","B1":"Score","A2":"Alice","B2":42}}},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L1.002","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"basic_cells_no_styles"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that creates an xlsx file at `path` using `openpyxl`. The workbook has one sheet named 'Inventory' with header row in row 1: A1='SKU', B1='Quantity'. Two data rows: A2='SKU-001', B2=10; A3='SKU-002', B3=25. Output ONLY the function definition inside a single ```python``` fenced block. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    from openpyxl import Workbook\n\n    wb = Workbook()\n    ws = wb.active\n    ws.title = 'Inventory'\n    ws['A1'] = 'SKU'\n    ws['B1'] = 'Quantity'\n    ws['A2'] = 'SKU-001'\n    ws['B2'] = 10\n    ws['A3'] = 'SKU-002'\n    ws['B3'] = 25\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","sheet_names":["Inventory"],"cells":{"Inventory":{"A1":"SKU","B1":"Quantity","A2":"SKU-001","B2":10,"A3":"SKU-002","B3":25}}},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L1.003","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"plain_text_only"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that creates an xlsx file at `path` using `openpyxl`. The workbook has one sheet named 'Scores' containing only the header row in row 1: A1='Player', B1='Wins', C1='Losses'. No data rows. Output ONLY the function definition inside a single ```python``` fenced block. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\n\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    wb = Workbook()\n    ws = wb.active\n    ws.title = 'Scores'\n    ws.append(['Player', 'Wins', 'Losses'])\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","sheet_names":["Scores"],"cells":{"Scores":{"A1":"Player","B1":"Wins","C1":"Losses"}},"exact_nonempty_cells":true},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L1.004","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"format":"docx","complexity":"plain_text_only"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_doc(path: str) -> None` that creates a DOCX file at `path` using `python-docx`. The document must contain exactly one paragraph. That paragraph's text must be exactly `Hello, world.`. Do not apply any direct character or paragraph formatting. Output ONLY the function definition inside a single ```python``` fenced block. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\ndef make_doc(path: str) -> None:\n    doc = Document()\n    doc.add_paragraph(\"Hello, world.\")\n    doc.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["docx"],"function":"make_doc","ooxml":{"kind":"docx","paragraphs":[{"text":"Hello, world.","style":"Normal","direct_formatting":false}],"tables":[]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L1.005","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L1","axis_values":{"format":"pptx","complexity":"plain_text_only"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_pres(path: str) -> None` that creates a pptx file at `path` using `python-pptx`. The presentation has one slide using the blank layout (layout index 6 from the default template) with no shapes added. Output ONLY the function definition inside a single ```python``` fenced block. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\n\ndef make_pres(path: str) -> None:\n    prs = Presentation()\n    prs.slides.add_slide(prs.slide_layouts[6])\n    prs.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["pptx"],"function":"make_pres","ooxml":{"kind":"pptx","slides":[{"layout_index":6,"layout_has_title":false,"title":null,"extra_shapes":0}]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L2.001","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"with_formulas_or_styles"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that creates an xlsx file at `path` using `openpyxl`. Sheet 'Calc' contains: A1=10, A2=20, A3=30, A4 contains the formula `=SUM(A1:A3)` (stored as a formula string starting with '='). Output ONLY the function inside a ```python``` fence. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\n\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    wb = Workbook()\n    ws = wb.active\n    ws.title = 'Calc'\n    ws['A1'] = 10\n    ws['A2'] = 20\n    ws['A3'] = 30\n    ws['A4'] = '=SUM(A1:A3)'\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","required_sheet_names":["Calc"],"cells":{"Calc":{"A1":10,"A2":20,"A3":30,"A4":"=SUM(A1:A3)"}}},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L2.002","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"with_formulas_or_styles"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` using `openpyxl` that creates an xlsx file at `path`. The workbook must contain a sheet named `Header`. In that sheet, cell `A1` must have the value `Title` and its font must have `bold=True`. Output exactly one ```python``` code fence containing only the necessary Python imports and the `make_workbook` definition; no other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font\n\n\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    wb = Workbook()\n    ws = wb.active\n    ws.title = \"Header\"\n    ws[\"A1\"] = \"Title\"\n    ws[\"A1\"].font = Font(bold=True)\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","required_sheet_names":["Header"],"cells":{"Header":{"A1":{"value":"Title","font":{"bold":true}}}}},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L2.003","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"format":"pptx","complexity":"with_formulas_or_styles"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_pres(path: str) -> None` that creates a PPTX file at `path` using `python-pptx`. The presentation must contain exactly one slide created with a slide layout that has a title placeholder. Set that title placeholder's text exactly to `Welcome`. Output ONLY the function inside a ```python``` fence. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\n\n\ndef make_pres(path: str) -> None:\n    prs = Presentation()\n    slide = prs.slides.add_slide(prs.slide_layouts[0])\n    slide.shapes.title.text = \"Welcome\"\n    prs.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["pptx"],"function":"make_pres","ooxml":{"kind":"pptx","slides":[{"layout_has_title":true,"title":"Welcome"}]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L2.004","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"format":"docx","complexity":"with_formulas_or_styles"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_doc(path: str) -> None` that creates a docx at `path` using `python-docx`. The document contains exactly one paragraph with the text `Important Notice` and styled with the `Heading 1` style. Output ONLY the function inside a ```python``` fence. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\ndef make_doc(path: str) -> None:\n    doc = Document()\n    doc.add_paragraph(\"Important Notice\", style=\"Heading 1\")\n    doc.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["docx"],"function":"make_doc","ooxml":{"kind":"docx","paragraphs":[{"text":"Important Notice","style":"Heading 1"}],"tables":[]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L2.005","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L2","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"with_formulas_or_styles"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that uses `openpyxl` to create and save an XLSX workbook at `path`. The workbook must contain exactly two worksheets, in this order: `Q1` and `Q2`. Set `Q1!A1` to `Revenue`, `Q1!B1` to numeric value `100`, `Q2!A1` to `Revenue`, and `Q2!B1` to numeric value `120`. Output only the function in a ```python``` fence. The evaluation system extracts Python code from that fence before execution.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\n\n\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    wb = Workbook()\n    q1 = wb.active\n    q1.title = \"Q1\"\n    q1[\"A1\"] = \"Revenue\"\n    q1[\"B1\"] = 100\n\n    q2 = wb.create_sheet(\"Q2\")\n    q2[\"A1\"] = \"Revenue\"\n    q2[\"B1\"] = 120\n\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","sheet_names":["Q1","Q2"],"cells":{"Q1":{"A1":"Revenue","B1":100},"Q2":{"A1":"Revenue","B1":120}}},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L3.001","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"format":"docx","complexity":"with_charts_or_embeds"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_doc(path: str) -> None` that creates and saves a DOCX file at `path` using `python-docx`. The document must contain exactly the following content in this order, with no additional paragraphs or tables: (1) a paragraph with style `Heading 1` and text `Report`; (2) a paragraph with style `Normal` and text `Summary follows.`; (3) one 2x2 table whose row-major cell texts are `A`, `B`, `C`, `D`. Output only the function in a ```python``` fence, with no other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n\ndef make_doc(path: str) -> None:\n    doc = Document()\n    doc.add_paragraph('Report', style='Heading 1')\n    doc.add_paragraph('Summary follows.', style='Normal')\n    table = doc.add_table(rows=2, cols=2)\n    values = [['A', 'B'], ['C', 'D']]\n    for r, row in enumerate(values):\n        for c, value in enumerate(row):\n            table.cell(r, c).text = value\n    doc.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["docx"],"function":"make_doc","ooxml":{"kind":"docx","paragraphs":[{"text":"Report","style":"Heading 1"},{"text":"Summary follows.","style":"Normal"}],"tables":[[["A","B"],["C","D"]]]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L3.002","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"with_charts_or_embeds"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that creates an xlsx at `path` using `openpyxl`. Sheet 'Chart' has headers in row 1: A1='Quarter', B1='Sales'. Data in rows 2-5: (Q1,100), (Q2,150), (Q3,120), (Q4,200). Add a BarChart object that references B1:B5 as the data series and A2:A5 as categories, and anchor it at cell 'D2'. Output ONLY the function inside a ```python``` fence. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\nfrom openpyxl.chart import BarChart, Reference\n\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    wb = Workbook()\n    ws = wb.active\n    ws.title = \"Chart\"\n    ws.append([\"Quarter\", \"Sales\"])\n    for row in [(\"Q1\", 100), (\"Q2\", 150), (\"Q3\", 120), (\"Q4\", 200)]:\n        ws.append(row)\n\n    chart = BarChart()\n    data = Reference(ws, min_col=2, min_row=1, max_row=5)\n    categories = Reference(ws, min_col=1, min_row=2, max_row=5)\n    chart.add_data(data, titles_from_data=True)\n    chart.set_categories(categories)\n    ws.add_chart(chart, \"D2\")\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","required_sheet_names":["Chart"],"cells":{"Chart":{"A1":"Quarter","B1":"Sales","A2":"Q1","B2":100,"A3":"Q2","B3":150,"A4":"Q3","B4":120,"A5":"Q4","B5":200}},"charts":[{"sheet":"Chart","type":"BarChart","anchor":"D2","data":{"sheet":"Chart","min_col":2,"max_col":2,"min_row":1,"max_row":5},"categories":{"sheet":"Chart","min_col":1,"max_col":1,"min_row":2,"max_row":5},"titles_from_data":true}]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L3.003","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"format":"pptx","complexity":"with_charts_or_embeds"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_pres(path: str) -> None` that creates and saves a PowerPoint presentation at `path` using `python-pptx`. The presentation must contain exactly three slides. Each slide must use a layout with a title placeholder, and its title placeholder text must be exactly: slide 1: `Intro`; slide 2: `Body`; slide 3: `End`. Output ONLY the function inside a ```python``` fence. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\n\ndef make_pres(path: str) -> None:\n    prs = Presentation()\n    for title in (\"Intro\", \"Body\", \"End\"):\n        slide = prs.slides.add_slide(prs.slide_layouts[0])\n        slide.shapes.title.text = title\n    prs.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["pptx"],"function":"make_pres","ooxml":{"kind":"pptx","slides":[{"layout_has_title":true,"title":"Intro"},{"layout_has_title":true,"title":"Body"},{"layout_has_title":true,"title":"End"}]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L3.004","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"format":"docx","complexity":"with_charts_or_embeds"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_doc(path: str) -> None` that creates and saves a valid DOCX file at `path` using `python-docx`. The document must contain exactly four non-empty paragraphs in this order: (1) a paragraph with text `Items` styled `Heading 1`; (2) `Apple` styled `List Bullet`; (3) `Banana` styled `List Bullet`; and (4) `Cherry` styled `List Bullet`. Output only the function in a ```python``` code fence, with no explanatory text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n\ndef make_doc(path: str) -> None:\n    doc = Document()\n    doc.add_paragraph(\"Items\", style=\"Heading 1\")\n    for item in (\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Cherry\"):\n        doc.add_paragraph(item, style=\"List Bullet\")\n    doc.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["docx"],"function":"make_doc","ooxml":{"kind":"docx","nonempty_paragraphs":[{"text":"Items","style":"Heading 1"},{"text":"Apple","style":"List Bullet"},{"text":"Banana","style":"List Bullet"},{"text":"Cherry","style":"List Bullet"}],"tables":[]},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
{"probe_id":"output.ooxml_authoring.L3.005","canonical_id":"output.ooxml_authoring","category":"output","level":"L3","axis_values":{"format":"xlsx","complexity":"with_charts_or_embeds"},"system_prompt":"","prompt":"Write a Python function `make_workbook(path: str) -> None` that creates an xlsx at `path` using `openpyxl`. The workbook has THREE sheets in this exact order: 'Summary', 'Details', 'Notes'. 'Summary' has A1='Total', B1 with formula `=Details!B2+Details!B3`. 'Details' has A1='Item', B1='Cost', A2='alpha', B2=10, A3='beta', B3=20. 'Notes' has A1='Reviewed by Finance.'. Output ONLY the function inside a ```python``` fence. No other text.","ground_truth":"```python\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\n\n\ndef make_workbook(path: str) -> None:\n    wb = Workbook()\n    summary = wb.active\n    summary.title = 'Summary'\n    details = wb.create_sheet('Details')\n    notes = wb.create_sheet('Notes')\n\n    summary['A1'] = 'Total'\n    summary['B1'] = '=Details!B2+Details!B3'\n\n    details['A1'] = 'Item'\n    details['B1'] = 'Cost'\n    details['A2'] = 'alpha'\n    details['B2'] = 10\n    details['A3'] = 'beta'\n    details['B3'] = 20\n\n    notes['A1'] = 'Reviewed by Finance.'\n    wb.save(path)\n```","scorer":{"type":"code_parse_ast","parser":"python","checks":{"import_prefixes":["openpyxl"],"function":"make_workbook","ooxml":{"kind":"xlsx","sheet_names":["Summary","Details","Notes"],"cells":{"Summary":{"A1":"Total","B1":"=Details!B2+Details!B3"},"Details":{"A1":"Item","B1":"Cost","A2":"alpha","B2":10,"A3":"beta","B3":20},"Notes":{"A1":"Reviewed by Finance."}}},"require_single_fenced_code":true}},"tags":["unit_test_required"],"notes":""}
